From 43d972b04cf5096bb6350f8aecb64320772ba3fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 08:29:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] dos: patch 0090 -- device-rate setter (productionize 0087
 as default-ON)

SDL/0087 landed the device-rate lever only as an env hint. This adds the ship
path so the SB16 PCM device opens at the content rate by default with no env
var, closing the v1.0.8 organya-delivery productionization.

New export SDL_DOSAudioSetDeviceFrameRate(int hz) on a new header
SDL_dosaudio_devicerate.h. SoundManager calls it with SAMPLE_RATE before
MIX_CreateMixerDevice (alongside SDL_DOSPixtoneSetMasterRate); the backend
caches it and applies it in OpenDevice. Opening at the content rate (11025
Tier-2) instead of SDL core's 44100 quality floor cuts the DMA ring drain 4x
and collapses the SDL logical->physical resampler to a cheap channel-dup --
the root of the organya slow-tempo/underrun behaviour on the 486 (delivery-
bound, not synth-bound; see docs/internal/V108-MUSIC-RETROSPECTIVE.md).

Precedence in OpenDevice: env hint SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_DEVICE_RATE
(0087) WINS (per-cell sweep override) > setter default > 44100 floor. A
killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_DEVICE_RATE_DEFAULT=0 (strict-"0")
disables the setter default for a clean A/B baseline cell. Out-of-band music
backends (OPL3/WaveBlaster) never touch this PCM path, so default-backend
audio is unchanged. Blast radius is the organya + Pixtone PCM path only.
Workspace-local; never upstreamed.
---
 include/SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_devicerate.h | 106 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c        |  63 ++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 167 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 include/SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_devicerate.h

